<title>USA: North American Vaccine buys Cephalon site.</title>
<headline>North American Vaccine buys Cephalon site.</headline>
<dateline>BELTSVILLE, Md. 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>North American Vaccine Inc said Friday it has definitively agreed to buy a pharmaceutical manufacturing facility from Cephalon Inc for about $25 million in cash and assumed lease obligations.</p>
<p>Cephalon used the site to make Myotrophin, a drug it is developing with Chiron Corp to treat amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, North American said.</p>
<p>North American said it will use the 35,000-square-foot facility in Maryland to make future vaccine products.</p>
</text>
